67.382, 67.75], ["comment", 67.919, 68.395], ["a", 68.395, 68.673], ["or", 68.673, 68.87], ["b", 68.87, 69.382]], "lines": [[0.0, 7.081, "The moon is falling. It hits in four days. Everyone's packing to run. I hatched an army to protect our planet instead."], [7.393, 16.702, "In this town, every kid gets an egg on their tenth birthday. Most hatch a spark that floats around your head. The mayor's son got a lightning bolt, and he hasn't shut up about it since."], [17.028, 23.799, "My egg sat in the window for a year. Cold. Kids called it a rock. The mayor's son borrowed it once, as a doorstop."], [24.069, 33.042, "This morning, it cracked down the middle. Out stepped a knight made of blue fire, taller than the castle gate. Then a giant made of storm clouds, with lightning for eyes."], [33.294, 34.891, "The whole square went silent."], [35.147, 38.303, "The king's plan was to hide in his basement. Mine was bigger."], [38.522, 44.242, "First, the giant tried to blow the moon away. It didn't even wobble. He blew the roof off the bakery instead."], [44.489, 52.007, "Then the knight threw his sword at it. It flew so high, it scratched the moon. Just a scratch. But for one second, the moon stopped."], [52.256, 55.119, "Then the sword came back down, right through the mayor's roof."], [55.373, 57.806, "So it can be cut. We just have to reach it."], [58.151, 66.573, "A, every kid in town gives up their spark to make the sword longer than the river. B, the giant builds a staircase of storm clouds, all the way up."], [66.825, 69.382, "Three days left. Comment A or B."]]}